# Web Awesome Pro is published only to Web Awesome's own registry.
#
# It lives here rather than at the repository root because this is the only half that needs
# it: `backend/` installs with no token at all, which is what lets a fork's backend pull
# request pass CI (#164). Moving the file moves the credential's blast radius with it.
#
# The token is read from the environment and MUST NOT be written here. This file is
# committed to a public repository.
#   local: export WEBAWESOME_NPM_TOKEN=...   (see .env.example)
#   CI:    repository secret of the same name
#
# `scripts/check-npmrc.mjs` fails the build if this value is ever anything but ${...}, and it
# scans every .npmrc in the repository so that moving one does not move it out of scope.
@awesome.me:registry=https://npm.webawesome.com/
//npm.webawesome.com/:_authToken=${WEBAWESOME_NPM_TOKEN}
